  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman in a kitchen, reacting with alarm as she pulls a hot pizza from an oven, with the text overlay reading: \"what's the difference between a jew and a pizza\" and \"a pizza doesn't scream in the oven.\" This is a clear example of antisemitic hate speech, using a dehumanizing and violent metaphor to equate Jewish people with inanimate objects (pizza) and imply that Jews are capable of screaming or suffering in an oven, referencing the Holocaust. The visual of the woman's distressed reaction is juxtaposed with the text to reinforce the hateful message. The meme is designed to provoke discomfort and spread harmful stereotypes, making it a hateful and antisemitic piece of content.",
